"[SubViewport] Isolates a rectangular region of a scene to be displayed "
"independently. This can be used, for example, to display UI in 3D space.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [SubViewport] is a [Viewport] that isn't a [Window], i.e. it "
"doesn't draw anything by itself. To display anything, [SubViewport] must "
"have a non-zero size and be either put inside a [SubViewportContainer] or "
"assigned to a [ViewportTexture].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [InputEvent]s are not passed to a standalone [SubViewport] by "
"default. To ensure [InputEvent] propagation, a [SubViewport] can be placed "
"inside of a [SubViewportContainer]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/SubViewport.xml doc/classes/Viewport.xml
